   "flags": {},
   "order": -1,
   "mode": 0,
   "title": "Read me",
   "properties": {
    "text": ""
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "CONCEPT -> VIDEO -- Wan 2.2 image to video, 14B (604.7s measured)\n\nFive seconds (81 frames at 16 fps) of the start image moving, as a\nWEBM and an animated WEBP under output/video/, plus the last frame as\na PNG.  Two fp8 experts take turns: high noise for the first ten\nsteps, low noise for the last ten.\n\nThe defaults are what ran on the reference 16 GB card on 2026-10-02:\n480x640, 20 steps, cfg 3.5, the lightx2v 4-step LoRAs in the graph at\nstrength 0, which the server skips.  At strength 1 (then set both\nsamplers to 4 steps, cfg 1, split at step 2) that card ran out of GPU\nmemory four times: merging a LoRA into fp8 weights needs float copies\nof each weight on the card, and there was no room.\n\nThe start image is squeezed to width x height.  480x640 keeps the 3:4\nof a 1104x1472 concept; square would flatten a standing figure, and\n624x832 with the LoRAs on ran out of memory in the forward pass\n(without them, not tried).\n\nWrite the MOTION in the prompt, not the subject again: what moves, how\nfast, and that the camera and background stay put.\n\nThis makes a video.  Nothing in this image turns it into a clip for a\nrig: docs/reference/video-mocap.md is the state of that.\n\n---\n\nWan 2.2 image-to-video, 14B, the two-expert fp8 route\ncomplete_workflow.json runs: the high-noise expert takes the\nfirst steps, the low-noise expert the rest, both on the 2.1 VAE.\nThe start image is squeezed to width x height, so 480x640 keeps\nthe 3:4 of a 1104x1472 concept. 81 frames at 16 fps is five\nseconds. The defaults are what ran on the reference 16 GB card\non 2026-10-02: 480x640, 20 steps, cfg 3.5, split at step 10,\nwith the lightx2v 4-step LoRAs (Apache-2.0, in the wan_i2v\ngroup) present but at strength 0, which the server skips\n(nodes.py, load_lora: strength 0 returns the model unchanged).\nThat run took 604.7 s on ComfyUI's own clock, VRAM peaked at\n14,876 MiB, and the expert sat only partly on the card: 9,259 MB\nloaded, 4,372 MB offloaded, in the server log. With the LoRAs at\nstrength 1 (then set both samplers to 4 steps, cfg 1, split at\nstep 2) the same card ran out of GPU memory four times that day:\nat 624x832 in the forward pass, and at 480x640 while merging the\nLoRA into the fp8 weights, which needs float copies of each\nweight on the card. 624x832 without the LoRAs was not tried.\nSaves a WEBM and an animated WEBP under output/video/, and the\nlast frame as a PNG. Nothing here extracts motion from the\nvideo: docs/reference/video-mocap.md is the state of that."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
